  "close_rendering": "The LORD is my shepherd, I shall not lack.",
  "whats_happening": "In four Hebrew words, the psalm says who the LORD is to the speaker, then what follows. No verb joins the first two words. The line has two halves, and almost everything the rest of the psalm says spells out the first. 'My shepherd' is a verb form, closer to 'the one shepherding me'. So the line is about what God does, more than a title.",
